rec.ttl [currently](https://github.com/RealEstateCore/rec/blob/6dfc0a9671636ca959834a50db45186f6f189231/Source/SHACL/RealEstateCore/rec.ttl) makes some statements about vocabulary from QUDT and GeoJSON. In the case of, for example, `qudt:hasQuantityKind`, these statements have quite drastic implications:

https://github.com/RealEstateCore/rec/blob/6dfc0a9671636ca959834a50db45186f6f189231/Source/SHACL/RealEstateCore/rec.ttl#L20-L24

This implicitly turns every subject of a `qudt:hasQuantityKind` statement (including all the named individuals defined by QUDT for units) into a class, causing a lot of bad punning, and every object in such a statement into an instance of the non-existent class identified by the IRI `<qudt:QuantityKind>`.

[QUDT](https://github.com/qudt/qudt-public-repo/blob/cc3b8a5b3c32ff0b470aba486adac62a9df69c53/schema/SCHEMA_QUDT-v2.1.ttl#L2525-L2531):

```ttl
qudt:hasQuantityKind
  a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://qudt.org/2.1/schema/qudt> ;
  rdfs:label "has quantity kind" ;
  rdfs:range qudt:QuantityKind ;
  owl:inverseOf qudt:isQuantityKindOf ;
.
```

I'd propose to remove all statements about foreign vocabulary entirely to avoid problems like these.

If you did want to implement a Firebase version check with the functionality described in my comment [here](https://github.com/inter-ops/Converter/pull/129#discussion_r1060723194), all you would need to do is set the variable in the comment below.

The rest is all setup! To test said functionality, just go to `Firebase → Simulate Lower App Version` in the `Debug` menu!

**Current Logic Summary**
```swift
if firebaseVariable != nil {
  if appVersion < firebaseVariable {
    // disableUI and show alert leading to Mac App Store page
  }
}
// else, do nothing
```

Setting the Firebase variable to `1.1` is all we'd need to do until a cracked version is published. If testing this variable in the app, be sure to update the version number under project settings first (it's always set to `1.0` until published).

